scripts/probe-v0.6.0.sh.findings — probe status
================================================
2026 record, branch v0.6.0-endpoint-probe (commit 2).

The probe script exists and passes `sh -n`, but it has NOT been executed:
FORGE_PROBE_HOST / FORGE_PROBE_TOKEN / FORGE_PROBE_REPO / FORGE_PROBE_PR are
unset in the implementation environment, so no live-instance findings exist.

Consequence for the probe-gated branches (E: Actions runs, G: issue lock,
H: notifications): per the probe-first rule in plans/releases/v0.6.0.md,
these branches must cite probe findings before their transports are trusted.
Until this script is run against the live instance and the labeled finding
lines are recorded here (or in the release doc), the wire encodings in
E1/G1/H1 are contract guesses from plans/implementation/v0.6.0.md's
foundational contracts, and the "wire shape, probe finding, and commit
change together" amendment path applies at merge review.

How to run:
  FORGE_PROBE_HOST=git.ngenesis.co.uk \
  FORGE_PROBE_TOKEN=<token with repo write> \
  FORGE_PROBE_REPO=<owner>/<test repo> \
  [FORGE_PROBE_REF=main] [FORGE_PROBE_PR=<n>] \
  sh scripts/probe-v0.6.0.sh | tee scripts/probe-v0.6.0.sh.findings

Findings format: labeled lines "label: STATUS accepted|rejected excerpt".
